<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Carson returns nine days after presenting with a firm lump in the upper outer left breast. The diagnostic mammogram and ultrasound a week ago showed a 2.4 cm irregular spiculated mass at 2 o&apos;clock, BI-RADS 5, with normal axillary nodes. The ultrasound-guided core biopsy five days ago shows invasive ductal carcinoma, grade 2, ER 95 percent, PR 80 percent, HER2 1+ (negative), Ki-67 22 percent. Before the result was given she was asked what she wanted to know and how; she said she wanted all of it, plainly, and the report in her hand. She was told directly that the biopsy shows breast cancer, that it appears to be early and confined to the breast, and that the aim of treatment is cure. In her own words back she described an early cancer fed by estrogen, to be removed by surgery, with lymph node testing at the operation. She met Dr. Solís-Abernathy this morning and, after hearing the choice between breast-conserving surgery with radiation and mastectomy, chose breast-conserving surgery. She has no bone pain, cough, headache, or weight loss. Her ulcer pain has gone and she is taking omeprazole. She asked that her diagnosis be shared only with a close friend and her editor, and that she be the one to tell them. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Interval change</td><td>Imaging BI-RADS 5; core biopsy invasive ductal carcinoma, ER and PR positive, HER2 negative</td></tr><tr><td>Disclosure</td><td>Told the diagnosis in person in plain words; report copy given; teach-back correct</td></tr><tr><td>Her decision</td><td>Breast-conserving surgery with sentinel node biopsy, after both options were explained</td></tr><tr><td>Coordination</td><td>Breast surgical oncology seen this morning</td></tr><tr><td>Privacy</td><td>Diagnosis to be shared only with the two people she names, by her</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

